# Testing & Verification

## Commands (prefer scripts)

- Frontend lint: `cd frontend && yarn lint` (or npm).
- Backend tests: `cd backend && python -m pytest` (use scripts/test).
- Full gate: `scripts/verify`.

## Rules

- Do not claim PASS without running the command.
- If Emergent preview URLs are the default in a test, override with local `EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL` or skip live tests when offline.
- Add regression tests near the changed domain (`test_iter*` style is fine).
- After fixes: re-run the failing suite, then a focused regression set.

## Definition of verified

- Relevant pytest green (or failures explained as pre-existing with evidence)
- Lint clean or only pre-existing issues noted
- App/server started when the feature is runtime-visible
- Manual/API check of the user-facing flow documented in CHANGELOG_AI
